excerpt: The Kenya Medical Association has endorsed Dr. Bill Llia for Governor of Nairobi County, praising his two-decade track record in community health and his detailed healthcare platform.
---

NAIROBI — The Kenya Medical Association (KMA), the professional body representing over 5,000 medical practitioners nationwide, today endorsed Dr. Bill Llia for Governor of Nairobi County.

In a statement signed by KMA chairperson Dr. Faith Nyambura, the association cited Llia's two decades of service in community health and his detailed healthcare platform as the basis for their endorsement.

"Dr. Llia is not just a candidate who talks about healthcare — he is one of us who has spent his career delivering it in the communities that need it most," the statement read. "His plan for a community health center in every ward, combined with his commitment to fully staffing and stocking existing facilities, represents the most comprehensive healthcare platform of any candidate in this race."

The endorsement highlights specific aspects of Llia's healthcare plan:

- A community health center in every ward, bringing primary care within 30 minutes of every resident
- A county drug procurement reform to eliminate stock-outs at public health facilities
- A maternal health program targeting zero preventable maternal deaths in county facilities
- A partnership with the national government to expand health insurance coverage

"This endorsement carries the weight of medical professionals who have seen the state of healthcare in Nairobi County firsthand," Llia said in response. "I am deeply honored and committed to proving that their trust is well placed."

The endorsement is expected to carry significant weight with voters, particularly in urban and peri-urban areas where access to quality healthcare is a top concern.
